  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Little change to the forecast reasoning and\nsynoptic setups through the period. Where guidance is fairly \nwell clustered is with an amplified upper trough that will be \nshifting east out of the Central U.S. While there is still some \npotential for a cutoff low to develop, most guidance has now \ntrended towards more of a progressive and open wave as it moves \nthrough the Eastern U.S. Before that happens, low level flow \nwill be from a moist easterly direction over the next several \ndays, which will advect favorable regime for on and off light \nrain, esp for the coastal areas through Thursday. Continued to\nincrease pops a bit along the coast to account for isolated to \nwidely scattered showers, best chances during diurnal heating, \nthrough mid week. ENC will cont under influence of e to se flow\nand hence a daily chance for widely sct showers. Don't expect \nmuch in the way of accums, but enough to wet the ground in \nplaces, esp the further east in ENC.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Most guidance is now centering on the best \nchance of showers and even a few thunderstorms moving in Friday.\nPerhaps some WAA showers on Thu with warm front migrating\nthrough, as well as perhaps a rumble of thunder as well, but \nmain forcing mechanism for showers and storms arrives Friday \nahead of a cold front. Of note, some guidance shows anomalous \nmoisture and higher- than- normal instability for early \nNovember, as indicated by EFI highlighting CAPE vals nearing the\n80th percentile. This would support the potential of some \nhigher rainfall rates and totals should this materialize. A few \nstronger storms may even materialize if timing of showers \narrives in the afternoon coinciding with peak heating. The other\naspect of the forecast that appears to be coming more clear \nthis week is the potential for above to well above normal \ntemperatures, especially Wednesday and Thursday, and esp during \nthe overnight periods. While record highs may not be broken, \nwarming low- level thicknesses in advance of the approaching \ntrough should support highs warming into the 70s, with some low \n80s possible inland. Meanwhile, overnight lows are forecast to \nbe closer to our normal highs for this time of year. Some record\nwarm lows may be in jeopardy. For reference, normal highs are \n65-70 for early November, with normal lows in the 40s inland and\n50s along the coast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Better agreement amongst 00z model guidance \nwith fropa now late Friday, which will usher in a more \nseasonably dry airmass for the coming weekend. Return to mo \nsunny skies and highs in the 60s and lows generally in the 40s.",
